Here is Stage 2: Socioeconomic Population Strata (Pop Classes, Real Wages &
Living Standards).

What this fundamentally changes

  - Before: Population was just a flat number (2500 people). They didn't work
    jobs, didn't earn wages, and had no expenses.
  - Now: Every settlement’s population is broken down into 5 socioeconomic
    classes:
    1.  Serfs & Peasants (Farming, forestry, and mining labor)
    2.  Burghers & Artisans (Workshop manufacturing, forging, weaving)
    3.  Merchant Guilds (Trade caravans, market distribution, banking)
    4.  Clergy (Temples, parish relief, literacy)
    5.  Nobility (Landlords, estate owners, military retinues)
  - Real Wages & The Cost of Living Basket:
      - Each class has a monthly consumption basket (Peasants need Grain, Ale,
        Salt, and Timber; Nobles demand Wine, Silk, and Weapons).
      - If food or firewood prices surge, the Cost of Living rises.
      - We calculate each class’s Standard of Living (SoL):
        \text{Standard of Living} = \frac{\text{Average Monthly Income}}{\text{Cost of Living Basket}}
  - Organic Unrest & Revolts:
      - When SoL drops below subsistence (<0.80), smallfolk cannot afford bread.
        Unrest climbs organically.
      - If unrest crosses 75\%, peasants refuse to pay taxes and stage bread
        riots—not from a random scripted event, but because real wages collapsed
        below survival!

